// Propulsion. PLACEHOLDER NUMBERS, all for feel only: thrust, torque and rated speeds were set on 12 Oct 2026 for
// the agility target "Agile" (GDR-0042: Halvex Runner 90° in ~0.8 s, 0 → ~22 m/s in ~2.5 s; small ships
// snappier), about 16× the concept-board thrust; gimbal values are invented.
// Engines push towards the part's forward side and need open cells directly behind them; `gimbal` swings their
// thrust a few degrees to either side. `rated_speed` (GDR-0041): the thrust fades out as the ship's speed along
// the push direction approaches it, so the fastest engines pushing a way set the top speed that way. Gyros turn
// the ship without thrust; RCS pods fire a nozzle out of every side that is open to space.
// Power tier: everything that moves the ship is `Normal` (the default), so thrust and turning brown out together.
[
    (
        id: "thruster",
        name: "Thruster",
        summary: "A small engine that needs open space behind it.",
        tags: ["engine"],
